usage: measure_devloop.py [-h] --core CORE --old OLD
                          --host-mode {ReleaseFast,ReleaseSafe,Debug}
                          --evidence EVIDENCE --work WORK
                          [--sizes SIZES [SIZES ...]]
                          [--roles {old,core} [{old,core} ...]]
                          [--rounds ROUNDS] [--parallel-size PARALLEL_SIZE]
                          [--parallel-workers PARALLEL_WORKERS]
                          [--core-extra CORE_EXTRA] [--timeout TIMEOUT]

S4-X synthetic dev-loop receipts. Launch through build-slot.sh build. CPU-10
commands acquire the shared timing lock one at a time. Parallel cold release
compilation keeps the build wrapper's affinity and is a separate row. Every
source edit has a fresh, retained digest, so a prior whole-project verdict
cannot turn an edited request into an unchanged request. Both compiler hosts
must be built in the explicit --host-mode, normally ReleaseFast. Each command
has its own log. Unchanged requests get an additional process trace to prove
the absence of zig cc. A distinct fresh release edit is traced to capture the
actual unit compile commands; the edited module's -O3 command is replayed with
a fresh local Zig cache. A report identifying source_path and llvm_path is
needed if more than one unit compiles. No unit is selected by its measured
cost.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --core CORE
  --old OLD
  --host-mode {ReleaseFast,ReleaseSafe,Debug}
  --evidence EVIDENCE
  --work WORK
  --sizes SIZES [SIZES ...]
  --roles {old,core} [{old,core} ...]
  --rounds ROUNDS
  --parallel-size PARALLEL_SIZE
  --parallel-workers PARALLEL_WORKERS
  --core-extra CORE_EXTRA
  --timeout TIMEOUT
